# sh-to-py C2: review-and-fix driver
Part of the sh-to-py bash-to-Python migration (umbrella tracking issue links all parts).
**Goal**: Port the review-and-fix loop (apply accepted findings as fixes) as Python functions calling the C1 review engine in-process — no subprocess indirection between review and fix phases.
**Notes**: /implement Step 5 calls review-and-fix directly (no /review indirection) — that call becomes an in-process function call; only the .md entry point goes through cli.py. Harness test-review-and-fix.sh (3559) ports to pytest here.
**Dependencies (wired natively via /block-issue)**: C1b, B1, B2.
**Definition of done**: importable functions; CLI verbs in python/cli.py; direct call-site cutover (no shims); pytest replaces harness coverage; absorbed bash + harnesses deleted; stale-reference sweep; make lint + py-lint + py-test green.
