- Treat `NO_SKETCHES` as authoritative.
- Draft from repository inspection only.
- Build `python/review_and_fix.py` as the Python owner for the absorbed review-and-fix domain.
- Preserve current contracts before deleting shell:
- accepted-findings mode
- Step 5 loop, single-round mode, and `mav-apply`
- `STEP5_REVIEW_STATUS` final envelope
- full `step5_emit_final_envelope` terminal KV bundle
- single final Step 5 envelope in loop mode
- suppressed per-round `REVIEW_AND_FIX_*` KVs during Step 5 loop iterations
- structured loop handoff equivalent to `IRF_LAST_*`
- loop-mode infrastructure failures as structured returns, never bare process exits before final envelope
- `review-and-fix.env` persistence for round results
- `STEP5_REVIEW_LEDGER_*` KVs on `main-agent-vote-required`
- fail-open escalation ledger keys and execution-issues breadcrumbs
- review/fix stderr sidecar used as `--failure-detail-log`
- canonical Step 5 ledger dispatcher token alignment with stall recovery
- `REVIEW_AND_FIX_*` round KVs outside suppressed Step 5 loop contexts
- summary JSON schema version 3
- accumulated OOS artifacts
- pre-review untracked and HEAD snapshots
- dynamic archetype precedence
- degraded-round retry behavior
- degraded-retry prune-ledger clearing for unsettled statuses
- main-agent escalation statuses
- Step 5 progress and done marker lifecycle
- Step 5 timing marks and resume timing integration
- Step 7 commit token and timing side effects
- stall-recovery escalation recording on `coder-main-agent-required`
- pre-scout eligibility before forwarding `--pre-scouted-manifest`
- per-round `round-meta.json` writing before run-log flush
- best-effort review batch flushes on stall, cap, MAV, degraded terminal, and other terminal branches
- post-round gates for lint-fix attempt cap, bulk skip ratio cap, and `prune-skipped`
- `--prune-ledger` forwarding to review core
- Call `review_pipeline.review_core(core_args)` directly from Python.
- Do not shell out to `python3 cli.py review core`.
- Capture review-core contract output into `round-N/review-core.env`.
- Do not re-emit `REVIEW_CORE_*` KVs on Step 5 stdout.
- Parse review-core KVs from `review-core.env`, like the shell path does today.
- Set `IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR` around the in-process review-core call and restore the prior environment in `finally`.
- Only emit the selected Step 5 or review-and-fix envelope for the active mode.
- C1b may still delegate internally through `run_legacy()`.
- Add an explicit review-core capture and test injection seam before caller cutover.
- Implement it as a context manager or wrapper such as `review_core_capture(core_args, env_path, review_core_impl=None, implement_tmpdir=None)`.
- Allow pytest to monkeypatch or pass `review_core_impl`.
- Capture normal stdout and `logging_util.emit()` machine-contract output.
- Patch any module-level `emit` alias used by `review_pipeline.run_legacy()` so relayed legacy KVs go to the capture sink.
- Restore stdout, emit sinks, and environment after each review-core call.
- Write captured contract lines to `round-N/review-core.env`.
- Block captured `REVIEW_CORE_*` lines from the Step 5 contract stream.
- Keep non-review-core Step 5 KVs on the normal Step 5 stream.
- Use `proc.run()` only for real external boundaries:
- Cursor commands
- Codex commands through an existing authenticated launch path or an importable wrapper around it
- existing shell helpers not in this C2 scope
- stall-recovery reporting if no importable Python API exists
- reviewer-prune recording if no importable Python API exists
- `scripts/write-implement-round-meta.sh` unless an importable Python API already exists
- `run-log write-round` unless an importable Python API already exists
- Do not add `python/review_and_fix.py` to a blanket raw `codex exec` allowlist.
- Prefer small helper functions over a large class unless state passing becomes noisy.
