## Edge cases
- Preserve empty `LARCH_DYNAMIC_ARCHETYPES_MAX` behavior.
- Preserve `--dynamic-archetypes 0` as authoritative.
- Treat unreadable findings files as hard failures where the shell does today.
- Preserve parse-error behavior for `check-changes`: emit the three stable stdout keys and exit 0.
- Preserve `--strict` fail-closed behavior for git probe failures.
- Keep missing untracked and HEAD baselines as graceful degradation.
- Preserve clean working tree plus advanced HEAD detection.
- Preserve degraded-panel retry cap of one retry per round.
- Clear unsettled reviewer-prune rows after degraded retry paths that do not record terminal prune status.
- Preserve `mav-resume-past-cap` only when the prior round artifact exists.
- Preserve coder `main-agent-required` status as non-stalled handoff.
- Preserve `coder-main-agent-required` stall-recovery recording.
- Preserve `main-agent-vote-required` ledger-ready KVs.
- Preserve canonical dispatcher token alignment.
- Preserve fail-open escalation sidecar and fallback ledger behavior.
- Keep accepted OOS and skipped OOS accumulation stable.
- Keep security skipped findings out of accepted OOS output.
- Keep submodule scrub and revert behavior fail-closed.
- Keep Step 5 done-marker writes fail-open only if the current launcher does.
- Keep prompt-side resume behavior working when `CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT` is absent.
- Forward `--pre-scouted-manifest` only when both eligibility inputs pass.
- Never forward pre-scouted manifests in `mav-apply`.
- Preserve review-core `--prune-ledger` forwarding for every Step 5 round.
- Preserve `IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR` environment parity for in-process review core.
- Preserve round-meta availability for Review Phase Detail rendering.
- Preserve run-log artifact copies after every round.
- Preserve review batch flushes on early terminal branches.
- Preserve non-terminal `prune-skipped` continuation behavior below cap.
- Keep `REVIEW_CORE_*` KVs out of Step 5 stdout.
- Keep Step 5 loop mode to one final full `STEP5_REVIEW_STATUS` envelope.
- Preserve single-round invocation parity for `--round-num` direct calls.
- Keep MAV apply pre-coder head snapshots in the relocated snapshot directory.
- Preserve MAV apply `0444` head-file permissions.
- Preserve MAV apply skipped full tracked snapshot behavior.
- Preserve MAV apply `mav-apply-done` and `CODER_STATUS` stdout contract.
- Preserve Step 7 commit token and timing side effects.
## Failure modes
- Python rewrite can change stdout ordering. Pin important KV order in tests.
- In-process review-core can leak `REVIEW_CORE_*` KVs. Route every Step 5 review-core call through the capture helper and test Step 5 stdout.
- `review_pipeline.run_legacy()` can relay legacy KVs through `logging_util.emit()`. Capture the emit sink as well as stdout.
- Capture wrappers can leave global output state or environment mutated after failure. Restore sinks and `IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR` in `finally` and test failure cleanup.
- Direct function calls can leak quiet-mode state. Initialize quiet mode per CLI entry and avoid global mutable output state.
- Loop mode can emit per-round `REVIEW_AND_FIX_*` KVs. Suppress round KVs and hand off structured state to the final envelope.
- Loop-mode infrastructure failures can bypass final status if implemented as bare exits. Return structured failures and emit the final envelope first.
- Deleting single-round launcher behavior can break direct Step 5 invocations. Preserve `--mode single` and `--round-num` parity.
- MAV apply can break handoff gates if it writes pre-coder heads under the wrong directory. Pin relocated snapshot behavior.
- MAV apply can break consumers if it omits `mav-apply-done` or `CODER_STATUS`. Pin both stdout KVs.
- Degraded retries can leave stale reviewer-prune rows. Clear unsettled round rows and test the path.
- Early stall or cap exits can skip run-log batches. Port `flush_review_batches` and cover at least one early stall.
- Deleting shell harnesses before pytest parity can lose coverage. Port tests before deletion.
- Stale path literals can fail `lint-retired-scripts`. Run repo-wide stale-reference checks after every deletion batch.
- Codex dispatch can fail auth lint. Route through the authenticated helper or wrapper, not a blanket allowlist.
- Prompt fences can fail on resume if they bypass `larch-run.sh`. Keep `larch-run.sh` in prompt-side Step 5 loop, single-round, and MAV fences.
- Step 5 progress can remain stuck if done markers are not written on every exit path. Test success, failure, and fallthrough exits.
- Stall-recovery can lose escalation evidence if status branches are not ported exactly. Pin `coder-main-agent-required`, escalation failure, and `main-agent-vote-required` branches in tests.
- Dispatcher token drift can redact valid ledger tokens or reject escalation rows. Keep allowlist, emitted KVs, and record-escalation argv aligned.
- External coder launch behavior can drift. Keep argv-level tests for Cursor and authenticated Codex dispatch.
- Pre-scouted manifests can change review-core dynamic slot behavior if forwarded without eligibility. Test eligible, ineligible, and MAV cases.
- Missing `--prune-ledger` can break later-round pruning. Assert the argv on every Step 5 review-core call.
- Missing `round-meta.json` can hide Review Phase Detail. Assert meta is written before run-log flush.
- Missing post-round gates can change stall and continuation behavior. Test lint cap, bulk skip cap, and prune-skipped branches.
- Missing commit token or timing side effects can regress Step 7 reporting. Test `commit-fixes` side effects.
## Testing strategy
- Run focused pytest first:
- `python3 -m pytest python/test_review_and_fix.py`
- `python3 -m pytest python/test_review_pipeline.py`
- Run migrated Make targets:
- `make test-review-and-fix`
- `make test-review-and-fix-dispatch`
- `make test-review-and-fix-convergence`
- `make test-review-and-fix-parsers`
- `make test-review-and-fix-step5-starting-round`
- `make test-run-step5-review`
- `make test-record-implement-review-round-timing`
- `make test-review-implement-step5-loop-timing`
- `make test-check-review-changes`
- `make test-commit-review-fixes`
- `make test-write-rejected-findings`
- token-propagation Make target if retained
- Run stale-reference checks:
- `git grep -n -E 'run-step5-review|review-and-fix\.sh|review-implement-step5-loop|record-implement-review-round-timing|check-review-changes\.sh|commit-review-fixes\.sh|write-rejected-findings\.sh'`
- Review every tracked hit outside archived logs and `python/migrated-scripts.tsv`.
- `make lint-retired-scripts`
- `make lint-codex-exec-auth`
- Run structural and docs sync checks:
- `bash scripts/test-implement-structure.sh`
- `bash scripts/test-review-structure.sh`
- `bash scripts/test-prompt-template-invariants.sh`
- `bash scripts/test-quick-mode-docs-sync.sh`
- Run required repo checks:
- `make py-lint`
- `make py-test`
- `bash scripts/relevant-checks.sh`
- `make lint`
